<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>SkyShift.Application</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SkyShift.Domain\SkyShift.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Teacher requirement: replaces the plain, manual, field-by-field
         "new XResponse { ... }" Entity to DTO copies in the Use Cases with
         AutoMapper, where those copies are a pure 1:1 property match. See
         Mapping/MappingProfile.cs for exactly which ones.

         Pinned at 12.0.1 deliberately, not left behind by accident. 12.0.1
         is affected by GHSA-rvv3-g6hj-g44x / CVE-2026-32933, a denial of
         service via uncontrolled recursion when mapping deeply nested
         object graphs. The only versions that contain the fix (15.1.1+ or
         16.1.1+) are also the first versions under AutoMapper's new RPL-1.5
         plus commercial dual license, which made AddAutoMapper's signature
         a breaking change (it now requires an
         Action of IMapperConfigurationExpression as its first argument, to
         carry a license key) plus a new MapperConfiguration constructor
         requirement. That is not a safe drop-in version bump, and it is not
         something verifiable from this environment, which has no
         dotnet/NuGet access to actually build and run a newer version.
         Practically, this project's exposure is low regardless: every
         CreateMap in MappingProfile.cs maps a flat Domain entity with only
         scalar properties, never a self-referencing or deeply-nested graph,
         to a DTO, and AutoMapper here only ever runs on trusted, already
         persisted Domain data on the way out to a response, never on
         client-supplied input, so the recursion-depth DoS has no reachable
         trigger in this codebase's actual usage. See the AutoMapper-upgrade
         task's report for the full analysis. -->
    <PackageReference Include="AutoMapper" Version="12.0.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
